From: TNG Technical Manual compatibility investigation
Subject: [PATCH] DIRECTOR: clear deactivated Trek Tech panorama frame

Trek Tech's QTVR panorama draws directly into the Director window surface.
Deactivating the panorama stops further input and decoding, but leaves its
last frame on that surface.  After a detail has been enlarged, reduced, and
closed, reopening the detail can therefore leave the restored panorama above
the newly prepared paused QuickTime detail frame.

When Trek Tech deactivates an active panorama, clear only the panorama's own
movie rectangle and mark the window dirty.  The title immediately paints the
next detail, transit, or restored panorama into that rectangle.  QTVR objects,
other games, activation, hotspot dispatch, and the rest of the stage are
unchanged.
---
 engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp b/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp
--- a/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp
+++ b/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp
@@ -360,8 +360,25 @@ void QTVR::m_setActive(int nargs) {
 	ARGNUMCHECK(1);
 
 	QTVRXObject *me = (QTVRXObject *)g_lingo->_state->me.u.obj;
 
-	me->_active = (g_lingo->pop().asInt() != 0);
+	bool active = g_lingo->pop().asInt() != 0;
+
+	// QTVR panoramas draw directly into the Director window surface. Trek
+	// Tech deactivates its panorama before replacing it with a paused detail
+	// movie, but the panorama's final pixels otherwise remain above that movie
+	// after an enlarge/reduce and return cycle. Clear only the outgoing movie
+	// rectangle; the title immediately repaints that area with its next view.
+	if (me->_active && !active && me->_video &&
+			me->_video->getQTVRType() == Common::QuickTimeParser::QTVRType::PANORAMA &&
+			Common::String(g_director->getGameId()).equals("trektech")) {
+		Window *window = g_director->getCurrentWindow();
+		if (window && window->getSurface()) {
+			window->getSurface()->fillRect(me->_rect, 0);
+			window->setDirty(true);
+		}
+	}
+
+	me->_active = active;
 }
 
 void QTVR::m_setHPanAngle(int nargs) {
